{"chunk_id": "c53af547cbe1", "text": "As the armies of Kurukshetra stand ready to clash, Yudhishthira performs a startling act: he removes his armor, lays aside his weapons, and walks unarmed into the enemy ranks. His brothers are alarmed, but Krishna explains that the king intends to seek the blessings of his elders before fighting. Yudhishthira respectfully approaches Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, and Salya, asking permission to wage war without incurring sin and even inquiring how they might be defeated. Each elder admits he is bound to fight for the Kauravas because of obligations and wealth, yet blesses Yudhishthira and reveals hints about his own vulnerability. Krishna also tries to recruit Karna, who refuses out of loyalty to Duryodhana. Meanwhile, Yuyutsu defects to the Pandava side. Yudhishthira\u2019s humility and adherence to dharma impress both armies, turning a moment before battle into a powerful moral statement.\nBefore battle, Yudhishthira seeks blessings and strategic insights from Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, and Salya; Karna refuses Krishna\u2019s offer; Yuyutsu defects to the Pandavas.\nThemes: dharma before battle, loyalty vs obligation, respect for elders, strategic foreknowledge, defection and allegiance", "vector": [0.0028080204501748085, -0.03127548098564148, -0.00914660282433033, 0.015101282857358456, -0.0028029910754412413, 0.035137973725795746, -0.020345155149698257, -0.0057199797593057156, -0.01667042076587677, -0.026930173859000206, 0.024998925626277924, -0.0034266230650246143, 0.01251958031207323, 0.006564900279045105, 0.002227975521236658, -0.003969786688685417, 0.04272885248064995, -0.0006680574151687324, 0.04160229116678238, -0.010903501883149147, -0.007020889315754175, -0.01622784323990345, 0.0038893178571015596, 0.01746169663965702, -0.025441503152251244, 0.013719904236495495, 0.018762605264782906, -0.01878942921757698, -0.001966452458873391, -0.024422233924269676, -0.009334363043308258, 0.004442539997398853, -0.0008172597154043615, -0.0042178